# Real, human-provided community sentences and anything derived from them
# (translations, latency numbers, adequacy ratings/notes) are never tracked,
# regardless of the fact that FLORES-derived results might be mixed in
# alongside them in the same file -- these three files are never committed,
# under any circumstance. See services/ai/mt/bakeoff/README.md.
#
# flores_samples.json (public FLORES-200 benchmark data) and
# community_samples_template.txt (empty template, no real content) are NOT
# covered by this ignore and are committed normally.
community_samples.txt
results.json
ratings.json
